              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for to suffer, then the Gujarati for to faint."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ગોળી",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ગોળી — goḷī — \"pill, tablet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હું રાત્રે ગોળી નથી લેતો. — hũ rātre goḷī nathī leto — \"I don't take the pill at night.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ગોળી (goḷī) is a tadbhava. It comes from Sanskrit gola, \"ball\", through golikā, \"little ball\", and CDIAL glosses the Gujarati word \"pill\" (CDIAL 4321)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
            }
          ]
        },
